special_abilities:
  - name: "Life Sense"
    description: "As every Lemurian. Reaches a 25 foot (7.6 m) radius plus 5 feet (1.5 m) per level. Locating, tracking or finding one particular kind of animal or plant is a roll at 20% plus 5% per level, with a further +5% underwater. The Lemurian racial description has the whole rule."
  - name: "Empathy with Animals"
    description: "As every Lemurian: animals of every kind take to the character at once. Monsters, predators and sentient creatures are the exceptions."
  - name: "Ley Line Powers"
    description: "As every Lemurian. On a ley line or at a stone pyramid the character heals and regains P.P.E. at twice a normal human''s rate, and swims 25% faster when following a ley line."
  - name: "Natural Abilities"
    description: "The same natural abilities as all Lemurians; see the Lemurian racial description."
  - name: "Ultrasonic Communication"
    description: "As every Lemurian: hears and produces high-frequency sound to talk with. It carries 2,000 feet (610 m) underwater and 400 feet (122 m) on the surface or in the air."
  - name: "Pets and Familiars"
    description: "A Scout usually travels with two animal companions, one small and one medium to large - typically a lemur or Aquatic Lemur and a land animal such as a dog, fox, wolf or a hunting cat (puma, lynx, lion and the like). The Scout also has a Lemurian War Steed of the player''s choice that can travel on land and in water."
  - name: "Trail Blazing"
    description: "Cuts and marks a trail through wilderness so that others can follow it, using ordinary trail signs, enchanted signals and psychic traces. Base skill 45% plus 5% per level. On a failed roll the trail cannot be followed as intended."
  - name: "Cross-Country Pacing"
    description: "Base skill 35% plus 5% per level. The Scout paces exertion, speed, food and water over long distances on foot, mounted or by propulsion pack. On foot he can run cross-country at full speed for P.E. x5 minutes without overexerting; in water he can swim at full speed for a time equal to P.E. x6. At half his maximum speed, with breaks, food and water, he can keep going for days. Used with Undersea or Land Navigation he can predict how long a trip will take to within 2D6x10 minutes, or 6D6 hours in unfamiliar country; a trip with others in tow takes at least twice as long as travelling alone. He favours little-known canals, crevasses, waterways and shortcuts over sea lanes, and does not show his best routes to clients or strangers short of an emergency."
  - name: "Cartography"
    description: "Mapmaking, with pen and paper, computer plotting or holographic display (computer mapping needs the Computer Operation skill). Base skill 40% plus 5% per level. A success gives a map that is accurate, easy to use and handsome; a failure gets some details wrong, leaves others out, and puts the scale and marked locations off by 1D10 miles. It also carries the equivalent of Basic Math at a fixed 50% plus any I.Q. bonus, or gives +5% to Mathematics: Basic if that is also taken as an O.C.C. Related Skill - which matters mostly to non-Lemurians, since every Lemurian already has Basic Mathematics."
  - name: "Perception: Nature, Hunting and Tracking"
    description: "+2 on Perception Rolls that involve nature, hunting and tracking. Conditional, so it is not in the stored bonuses."
restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any, as per Lemurians, so typically good."
  - "Racial requirements: none. The class is written for Lemurians all the same - its Skills Known by All Lemurians and its Lemurian R.C.C. abilities are printed inside the O.C.C. and are stored here as printed."
  - "Attribute requirements: I.Q. 8 and P.E. 12 or higher. A high P.S. and M.E. help but are not required."
  - "Secondary Skills: none. They are replaced by the Area of Specialty Skill Package."
  - "Espionage skills come only through a Specialty Skill Package; Electrical skills are not available at all."
  - "Holistic Medicine taken as an O.C.C. Related Skill counts as two skill selections."
  - "Ranger package, Hand to Hand: the page (printed 79) says only that Expert may become Martial Arts for one O.C.C. Related Skill ''or one of the above'', and does not say what ''the above'' refers to. One related skill is the price stored."
  - "Cybernetics: none. Lemurians have no interest in bionics, not even Bio-Systems."
  - "Savings: besides the starting money, 2D6x1,000 credits worth of artifacts, works of art and items from other cultures, probably kept safely at home. The starting 1D6x1,000 may be Universal Credits, gems and/or trade goods."
  - "Salary: 1,500 credits or trade goods a month if working for the Lemurian government or military. Otherwise the Scout lives off the land."
  - "War Steed: one animal suitable for land and water travel, or instead a horse or similar surface animal and a pack horse or mule, plus the two animal companions. Steeds and companions are creatures, not gear, and are not in the equipment list."
  - "Also carried and not in the equipment list because the catalog has no row for them: a mess kit, 2D6+6 plastic specimen bags, and various common personal items."
  - "Assignments: a particular mission or posting can come with extra or specialised weapons and gear, issued for the job (printed 80)."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria, printed 77-80, under the section heading
    "Lemurian Adventurer O.C.C.". Printed 78 is a full-page illustration; the
    entry ends on printed 80 (equipment, Cybernetics and Money), a page past
    where the Stats block starts.
  - NO `sdc_base` AND NO `mdc_base`, so the class carries `men_of_arms: false`:
    the book files it under "Lemurian Adventurer O.C.C.", not under "Lemurian
    Men-At-Arms O.C.C.s". `occ_group: optional` for the same reason. The
    +2D6+6 "physical S.D.C." of printed 77 is a pool bonus on top.
  - `xp_table` is the "Sea Sentinel & Lemurian Scout" ladder on the Experience
    Tables, printed 86, read off a render of the page: each entry is the lower
    bound of its band.
  - THE AREA OF SPECIALTY SKILL PACKAGE IS `skills.mos`, pick one of five
    (Explorer, Naturalist, Ranger, Treasure Hunter, Zoologist; printed 79-80).
    Each package''s Hand to Hand style is a skill inside the package.
  - A PACKAGE LINE OFFERING TWO SKILLS AT DIFFERENT BONUSES STORES THE LOWER.
    The book prints seven such lines - Barter (+10%) or Archaeology (+15%);
    Carpentry (+20%) or Escape Artist (+10%); Prowl (+10%) or Boat Building
    (+20%); Track & Hunt Sea Animals (+15%) or Track & Trap Animals (+20%);
    Preserve Food (+20%) or Undersea Farming (+10%); Xenology (+10%) or Medical
    Doctor (+5%); and among the O.C.C. skills Horsemanship: General (+5%) or
    Pilot Paddle-Type Boats (none). A pick group holds one bonus for every
    option, so each stores the lower figure (none, for the last) and its note
    names the difference to add by hand.
  - THE HAND TO HAND PRICES DIFFER BY PACKAGE AND ONE BLOCK HOLDS THEM ALL.
    Printed 79-80: Explorer is Expert, Martial Arts (or Assassin if evil) for
    two related skills; Naturalist, Treasure Hunter and Zoologist are Basic,
    Expert for one; Ranger is Expert, Martial Arts for one related skill "or
    one of the above". Stored as expert 1, martial_arts 1, assassin 2 with the
    package named in each condition. Martial Arts is priced at the Ranger''s
    one; the Explorer''s second related skill is charged by hand. The page
    does not say what "the above" refers to, and no reading of it is stored.
  - "AQUATIC: ANY (+10%)" HAS NO CATALOG CATEGORY. Stored as one related-skill
    entry named Aquatic at +10 whose `only` list is the book''s Aquatic Skills
    list (printed 54) by catalog name. Left out of it: the six this class
    already grants as O.C.C. skills (Language: Lemurian, Language: Oceanic,
    Horsemanship: Sea Monsters, Lore: Sea Creatures, Navigation: Underwater,
    Undersea & Sea Survival) and Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter, which is the
    Serpent Hunter''s own. Track & Hunt Sea Animals is also inside Wilderness,
    which this class prints at +15%, and the two aquatic languages are also
    covered by the +10% on any Language.
  - "COMMUNICATIONS: ... LANGUAGE (ANY; +10%), LITERACY (ANY)". The catalog
    files languages, and some literacies, under Technical, which this class
    also has as "Any"; the language +10% is on the Technical bonus entry.
  - PILOT AND PILOT RELATED EXCLUSIONS ARE PARTLY PROSE. "Robots, power armor,
    military" is stored as an exclusion of Robots & Power Armor, every Robot
    Combat row and every Military: row. "Large, noisy vehicles" and Pilot
    Related''s "military vehicles and giant robots" name no catalog rows and
    are in the category notes for the player to honour.
  - "Gambling" is stored as both catalog rows, Standard and Dirty Tricks.
  - SKILLS KNOWN BY ALL LEMURIANS ARE STORED ON THE O.C.C., as printed in its
    own Stats block (printed 79), although Racial Requirements is "None".
    Swimming is this class''s own figure, 76% +2% per level. Literacy: Lemurian
    is the catalog row of that name, at the printed 85% +1%. Lemurian and
    Oceanic are printed "at 96%" with no rate; the +1% per level is the
    native-speaker rate of the skill descriptions on printed 55.
  - TRAIL BLAZING, CROSS-COUNTRY PACING AND CARTOGRAPHY are printed as Special
    O.C.C. Abilities with a base skill and a per-level rate (45% +5%, 35% +5%,
    40% +5%; printed 77). The catalog holds no skill row for any of them, so
    they are `special_abilities` prose and are not on the skill list.
  - CONDITIONAL BONUS KEPT AS PROSE: +2 on Perception Rolls involving nature,
    hunting and tracking (printed 77).
  - EQUIPMENT. "Any 1D4+1 Symbiotic Bio-Constructs of choice that are not
    weapons" is a pick of two with the roll in its note. The sidearm and the
    knife or sword are catalog sets, since the book enumerates neither. Not
    stored for want of a catalog row: mess kit, 2D6+6 plastic specimen bags,
    satchel, water skin (the duffle bag and canteen stand for the pairs they
    are printed in). Substitutions by nearest row: box of wooden matches,
    fishing kit, collapsible pole, small flashlight, distance binoculars,
    laser distancer, sketchbook, pocket notebook, wide brim hat.
  - MONEY. `starting_money` is the 1D6x1,000 of printed 80; the 2D6x1,000 of
    savings is goods, and the 1,500 credit salary is conditional. Both are
    restriction lines.
