# Lemurian Scout

## Lore

Lemuria has come back into a world it barely knows, and the Scouts are the people it sends to find out what is there. They are as comfortable in deep water as any of their kind, but much of their work is done ashore, among surface peoples, where a Scout generally lets strangers take him for one more D-Bee or off-world visitor. When he would rather not be seen at all he goes back into the sea, or into the nearest river or lake.

Many of them are wanderers by temperament, called World Trekkers, Out-Reachers or Lemurian Wanderers, who travel for the love of wild places and of learning. On the way they help whoever needs it, fight monsters and the undead, and look after the living world one small disaster at a time. They carry Bio-Weapons, wear Bio-Armor, eat what nature provides, and pick up the odd useful tool or salvaged curiosity from the surface, but what they depend on is their own wits. They are tough, adaptable, curious about new peoples and ideas, and hold all life in high regard.

A Lemurian Scout is better schooled than a surface Wilderness Scout and has a field of his own: exploring, plants and herb lore, salvage and treasure hunting, the study of animals, or search, rescue and tracking.

## GM Notes

Scouts mostly work alone or in loose bands, but they keep an informal brotherhood and a network for trading information. It is led by Haumia-tiketike, who carries what the Scouts learn straight to the King of Lemuria.
